WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.238
- Hello Believe nation,

00:00:04.238 --> 00:00:05.580
today we're going to
talk about the seven ways

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.997
to have a true impact as an entrepreneur.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:13.494
- [computerized voice] Nine, eight.

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:16.657
Seven.

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:18.857
- So a theme that comes up a lot

00:00:18.857 --> 00:00:21.175
is that if you want to have
success as an entrepreneur

00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:23.373
the money can't be the
most important thing

00:00:23.373 --> 00:00:24.518
that you're going after.

00:00:24.518 --> 00:00:25.770
Money, yes, is important

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.126
but it can't be the number one.

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:28.465
If you look at the most successful people

00:00:28.465 --> 00:00:29.905
who've made a lot of money,

00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:31.544
money may be two or three on the list

00:00:31.544 --> 00:00:33.035
but number one there's something

00:00:33.035 --> 00:00:34.614
that's more important than money,

00:00:34.614 --> 00:00:36.612
and it's having that big impact.

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:38.724
So today I'm going to
talk about the seven ways

00:00:38.724 --> 00:00:42.141
to have a true impact as an entrepreneur.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.956
Number one is you need
to find your one word.

00:00:45.956 --> 00:00:47.034
I know I wrote a book about it.

00:00:47.034 --> 00:00:49.707
I know it sounds a little bit
self-serving, but it's true.

00:00:49.707 --> 00:00:52.459
You have to find the
thing that drives you.

00:00:52.459 --> 00:00:53.789
You have to have the self-awareness

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:56.376
to know what it is that you stand for.

00:00:56.376 --> 00:00:58.330
What is the impact that you want to have?

00:00:58.330 --> 00:00:59.828
That's what it's all about.

00:00:59.828 --> 00:01:01.455
You can't just say you
want to have an impact

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:02.886
but then not have a plan, right?

00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:06.509
You need to know what the
impact is that you want to have.

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:08.349
So for me, I want to spread more belief.

00:01:08.349 --> 00:01:10.125
I want people to believe in themselves.

00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:12.417
I want people to believe in
the work that they're doing.

00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:14.585
I want people to believe
that it's going to work out,

00:01:14.585 --> 00:01:16.377
and to keep on hustling,
and keep on trying,

00:01:16.377 --> 00:01:18.374
and keep adding that perseverance.

00:01:18.374 --> 00:01:21.561
You need to know what you stand for.

00:01:21.561 --> 00:01:23.523
You need to know what your one word is

00:01:23.523 --> 00:01:27.269
so you can go out and
create an amazing impact

00:01:27.269 --> 00:01:30.763
that has clarity and focus and purpose.

00:01:30.763 --> 00:01:32.936
Too many people want to have a big impact

00:01:32.936 --> 00:01:35.790
but they have no idea what
that big impact looks like.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.230
And so you're never going to get there.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.661
So you need to find your one word.

00:01:38.661 --> 00:01:41.034
You need to understand what
your main core value is

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:44.451
and what that impact actually looks like.

00:01:46.842 --> 00:01:48.610
Number two is identify your niche.

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:49.980
Once you know what your one word is,

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.256
once you know your value
that you're trying to create

00:01:52.256 --> 00:01:54.179
out there in the world and spread more of,

00:01:54.179 --> 00:01:56.602
you have to figure out where
you're going to attack.

00:01:56.602 --> 00:01:58.152
What's the niche that
you're going to attack?

00:01:58.152 --> 00:01:59.597
So for me, it's entrepreneurs.

00:01:59.597 --> 00:02:03.758
If you want to be the
world's greatest saxophonist,

00:02:03.758 --> 00:02:07.879
I can believe in you as
much as I want to, right?

00:02:07.879 --> 00:02:09.056
And that can help you.

00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:10.661
There'll be some value add there, right?

00:02:10.661 --> 00:02:14.087
Having a little injection of
belief is definitely valuable.

00:02:14.087 --> 00:02:16.338
But I don't know anything
about being a saxophone player.

00:02:16.338 --> 00:02:18.231
I can't give you specific knowledge.

00:02:18.231 --> 00:02:20.235
I don't have the context
to be able to help you.

00:02:20.235 --> 00:02:23.052
If you want to be an
entrepreneur, I know that.

00:02:23.052 --> 00:02:23.960
I've done that.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:24.793
I am that.

00:02:24.793 --> 00:02:25.626
I live that.

00:02:25.626 --> 00:02:26.524
I breathe that. I believe that.

00:02:26.524 --> 00:02:27.588
I do that every day.

00:02:27.588 --> 00:02:32.162
And so finding the niche helps
me have a greater impact.

00:02:32.162 --> 00:02:34.847
So just saying believe is great,

00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:36.400
and that can help people
believe in themselves,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.478
that's great.

00:02:37.478 --> 00:02:41.857
But I can have way more
power and way more impact

00:02:41.857 --> 00:02:44.394
and a way greater leverage on people

00:02:44.394 --> 00:02:46.256
when I know what I'm talking about.

00:02:46.256 --> 00:02:49.225
And so I can do that in the
world of entrepreneurship.

00:02:49.225 --> 00:02:50.601
I can do that in the world of salsa.

00:02:50.601 --> 00:02:53.284
I can kind of do that in the
world of League of Legends

00:02:53.284 --> 00:02:54.240
to some extent,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.177
a little bit in the world of baseball.

00:02:56.177 --> 00:02:57.460
Right, in some worlds.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:00.263
But entrepreneurship is where I reign.

00:03:00.263 --> 00:03:03.208
And so you need to understand
what your niche is as well.

00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:05.846
What is the audience
that you want to impact

00:03:05.846 --> 00:03:07.405
with your message?

00:03:07.405 --> 00:03:08.738
Find your niche.

00:03:12.041 --> 00:03:13.850
Number three is set a big goal.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:16.179
You want to have a big impact,
what does that look like?

00:03:16.179 --> 00:03:18.349
Again the more specific you can be

00:03:18.349 --> 00:03:20.044
the easier it's going
to be to motivate you

00:03:20.044 --> 00:03:21.704
to want to go out and do it.

00:03:21.704 --> 00:03:24.720
Right, if I say I want to
help a thousand entrepreneurs,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.373
that may not be the most
motivating of goals, right?

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:30.431
I'm not going to crawl
out of bed to say yes,

00:03:30.431 --> 00:03:35.079
my life's purpose is to help
a thousand entrepreneurs.

00:03:35.079 --> 00:03:36.943
Now, if I was helping them one on one,

00:03:36.943 --> 00:03:39.317
if I wanted to invest
in a thousand businesses

00:03:39.317 --> 00:03:42.023
and help those companies
really take off, then maybe.

00:03:42.023 --> 00:03:45.163
Maybe that is, to make a
thousand angel investments,

00:03:45.163 --> 00:03:46.350
that's no joke.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.399
That's a big deal.

00:03:47.399 --> 00:03:49.523
But my goal, I want to help
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:03:49.523 --> 00:03:51.007
I want to have a big reach.

00:03:51.007 --> 00:03:52.239
I want to make a big mark.

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:55.590
I want to have a big impact
on this world when I leave it.

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:56.995
It's not going to happen,

00:03:56.995 --> 00:03:58.751
I'm not hitting a billion people tomorrow,

00:03:58.751 --> 00:04:00.588
but I'm motivated by that.

00:04:00.588 --> 00:04:01.567
I'm driven by that.

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:02.905
I want to go out and accomplish,

00:04:02.905 --> 00:04:06.594
I want to do big things with
my message and abilities

00:04:06.594 --> 00:04:07.804
to be able to help people.

00:04:07.804 --> 00:04:10.126
And so having a big goal that you look at,

00:04:10.126 --> 00:04:12.618
that sometimes is scary,
sometimes you look at it

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.654
and say I don't know if I can do that.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.897
Those goals are important,
much more than having goals

00:04:17.897 --> 00:04:21.167
that are so low that you know you can hit

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.084
that don't really drive you forward.

00:04:23.084 --> 00:04:24.601
Les Brown was always famous for saying

00:04:24.601 --> 00:04:29.065
that most people don't set
goals that are too big and miss,

00:04:29.065 --> 00:04:32.047
they set goals that are
too low and they hit.

00:04:32.047 --> 00:04:33.727
And then you're complacent.

00:04:33.727 --> 00:04:35.670
You don't drive for more.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:40.004
So having a big goal that
gets you excited and scared

00:04:40.004 --> 00:04:43.768
and self doubt sometimes but motivated

00:04:43.768 --> 00:04:47.518
is important to be able
to have a big impact.

00:04:49.117 --> 00:04:50.743
Number four is then create a plan.

00:04:50.743 --> 00:04:52.061
Great to have a goal.

00:04:52.061 --> 00:04:55.473
Just like having your one
word, it's great to have that.

00:04:55.473 --> 00:04:56.916
Now you need to put the plan in place

00:04:56.916 --> 00:04:58.636
for how you're going to
go out and accomplish it.

00:04:58.636 --> 00:05:00.200
So you want to go help a billion people.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.325
You want to go make a
thousand angel investments.

00:05:02.325 --> 00:05:04.500
Whatever that goal looks like for you.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.064
What's your plan to then
go out and create it?

00:05:08.064 --> 00:05:09.813
And you may not have the perfect plan,

00:05:09.813 --> 00:05:12.781
and don't worry so much about
creating the perfect plan.

00:05:12.781 --> 00:05:14.027
A lot of people get held up here,

00:05:14.027 --> 00:05:17.305
in that they work so hard
on making the perfect plan

00:05:17.305 --> 00:05:19.025
they never do anything about it.

00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:21.140
But you need to have some kind of plan.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.310
You need to study success.

00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.802
You need to put in action what
you think is going to work,

00:05:24.802 --> 00:05:26.306
what logically makes sense,

00:05:26.306 --> 00:05:29.126
but you need to start
making the plan to go out

00:05:29.126 --> 00:05:33.293
and achieve that big goal
that you set for yourself.

00:05:34.781 --> 00:05:37.264
Number five is take consistent action.

00:05:37.264 --> 00:05:39.466
This is where a lot of people fall down.

00:05:39.466 --> 00:05:41.920
A lot of people have
big dreams, big goals,

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.723
but they're not consistent.

00:05:43.723 --> 00:05:47.456
They take a little bit of
action, maybe a lot of action,

00:05:47.456 --> 00:05:48.936
then they lose their motivation.

00:05:48.936 --> 00:05:51.081
They don't do anything for
a week, or a couple days.

00:05:51.081 --> 00:05:53.562
Then there's more
action, and then nothing.

00:05:53.562 --> 00:05:55.821
It's just constant start
and stop and start and stop

00:05:55.821 --> 00:05:57.493
and you never get anywhere.

00:05:57.493 --> 00:06:01.034
Right, you're in that car that
is just always on the brakes.

00:06:01.034 --> 00:06:04.701
You need consistent
action every single day,

00:06:05.773 --> 00:06:09.176
at least 30 to 60 minutes, ideally more

00:06:09.176 --> 00:06:13.208
but at least 30 to 60
minutes every single day

00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:16.906
on building your idea, on
building your business,

00:06:16.906 --> 00:06:19.640
on reaching for that big
impact that you are chasing.

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:20.473
It's important.

00:06:20.473 --> 00:06:22.964
You know when my YouTube
channel started taking off?

00:06:22.964 --> 00:06:25.212
When I started doing daily content.

00:06:25.212 --> 00:06:27.211
I used to be the guy who
was like oh once a week

00:06:27.211 --> 00:06:29.863
that's so much to make
one video a week is crazy.

00:06:29.863 --> 00:06:31.744
It's so much time, so much effort.

00:06:31.744 --> 00:06:34.446
It would be so much
easier to do one a month.

00:06:34.446 --> 00:06:36.600
And it's not until you make it a priority,

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.137
where you're doing it consistently.

00:06:38.137 --> 00:06:41.329
It's for any goal, it's
not just a business thing.

00:06:41.329 --> 00:06:43.172
You want to lose weight?

00:06:43.172 --> 00:06:45.289
You need to work out consistently.

00:06:45.289 --> 00:06:48.489
You need to eat healthy
consistently, right?

00:06:48.489 --> 00:06:50.094
You need to have the
plan, that's important,

00:06:50.094 --> 00:06:52.155
but you need to stick to the plan.

00:06:52.155 --> 00:06:53.908
You've got to do something about it

00:06:53.908 --> 00:06:57.995
and not just work out a
little bit and then stop.

00:06:57.995 --> 00:07:00.961
Eat healthy for a while and
then eat a bunch of crap.

00:07:00.961 --> 00:07:03.216
You're going to be constantly doing this

00:07:03.216 --> 00:07:04.780
and never actually making it grow.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.922
You want to have a great relationship?

00:07:06.922 --> 00:07:11.743
It's being consistently a
good husband, a good wife,

00:07:11.743 --> 00:07:14.179
a good boyfriend, a good girlfriend,

00:07:14.179 --> 00:07:16.123
a good father, a good mother.

00:07:16.123 --> 00:07:18.107
Right, it's not oh it's your birthday

00:07:18.107 --> 00:07:19.449
I'm going to get you flowers.

00:07:19.449 --> 00:07:21.948
Or once a month I'm
going to be nice to you.

00:07:21.948 --> 00:07:23.316
It's consistent.

00:07:23.316 --> 00:07:25.591
You want to have success in any field

00:07:25.591 --> 00:07:27.998
you need to take consistent action

00:07:27.998 --> 00:07:29.443
and that's one of the things

00:07:29.443 --> 00:07:31.485
where a lot of entrepreneurs fall down.

00:07:31.485 --> 00:07:32.666
You have great ideas.

00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:33.811
You have great ambition.

00:07:33.811 --> 00:07:35.111
You have great vision.

00:07:35.111 --> 00:07:37.379
You're just not consistent.

00:07:37.379 --> 00:07:40.629
You don't do the work every single day.

00:07:42.883 --> 00:07:44.512
Number six is build a team.

00:07:44.512 --> 00:07:46.389
This is really important
because you need to understand

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:48.724
that to do big things
you can't do it alone.

00:07:48.724 --> 00:07:52.132
It's so easy to want to be
the lone wolf entrepreneur,

00:07:52.132 --> 00:07:55.313
to feel like you can do everything
better than anybody else,

00:07:55.313 --> 00:07:57.505
and people that you've hired
before hasn't worked out

00:07:57.505 --> 00:07:59.540
so you're going to shrink back down

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.051
and do it all yourself again.

00:08:01.051 --> 00:08:02.370
That's what a lot of people do, right?

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.466
I'm ready to grow, okay great
I'm going to build a team,

00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:07.346
hire somebody, and that
person doesn't work out.

00:08:07.346 --> 00:08:09.086
So you think I'm never
going to hire anybody

00:08:09.086 --> 00:08:10.549
because that first one didn't work out,

00:08:10.549 --> 00:08:12.457
so I'm never going to hire anybody again.

00:08:12.457 --> 00:08:13.862
I'm just going to do it all myself.

00:08:13.862 --> 00:08:17.224
Right, well did your first
relationship work out?

00:08:17.224 --> 00:08:19.523
For some people yes, but most people no.

00:08:19.523 --> 00:08:21.015
You probably sucked as a manager.

00:08:21.015 --> 00:08:23.771
You probably hired the
wrong person to begin with.

00:08:23.771 --> 00:08:25.554
'Cause it's not just hiring for skills,

00:08:25.554 --> 00:08:27.010
you need to hire for values.

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:29.825
You probably didn't give them
enough time to train them

00:08:29.825 --> 00:08:30.830
and motivate them and encourage them

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.200
and understand who they are as a person.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:34.187
They may have sucked,

00:08:34.187 --> 00:08:36.620
but you probably equally sucked as a boss.

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.684
You learn through your relationships.

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:40.460
You learn through the hires you have.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.785
You learn through the
business that you create.

00:08:42.785 --> 00:08:44.439
And so you need to build a team.

00:08:44.439 --> 00:08:45.701
If you want to do something big,

00:08:45.701 --> 00:08:47.399
this really is about having a big impact,

00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:49.828
you cannot do it by yourself.

00:08:49.828 --> 00:08:51.842
You need to build a team.

00:08:51.842 --> 00:08:53.240
You need to focus on what is it

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:55.524
that you can bring genius level talent to,

00:08:55.524 --> 00:08:58.316
what are you among the best
people in the world at,

00:08:58.316 --> 00:09:02.243
and how can you spend as much
time doing that as possible

00:09:02.243 --> 00:09:05.800
and have the people on your
team doing everything else.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.169
Now you don't just start day one

00:09:07.169 --> 00:09:08.652
with a thousand people on your team.

00:09:08.652 --> 00:09:09.833
I get it.

00:09:09.833 --> 00:09:11.346
You may be starting by yourself.

00:09:11.346 --> 00:09:12.437
That's fine.

00:09:12.437 --> 00:09:15.064
But look for as soon as
possible to bring people on,

00:09:15.064 --> 00:09:16.298
whether it's an intern.

00:09:16.298 --> 00:09:17.233
I started with interns.

00:09:17.233 --> 00:09:18.790
I had high school interns.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.635
I had foreign language interns

00:09:20.635 --> 00:09:22.744
who wanted to learn
English and came to Canada

00:09:22.744 --> 00:09:26.878
and worked for me for free
for three to 12 months.

00:09:26.878 --> 00:09:28.206
I had high school interns

00:09:28.206 --> 00:09:29.941
who were getting a credit for their class

00:09:29.941 --> 00:09:32.217
and worked for me for a school year.

00:09:32.217 --> 00:09:33.823
Paid nothing.

00:09:33.823 --> 00:09:35.600
I had people on part time gigs.

00:09:35.600 --> 00:09:37.596
The first person I hired was part time,

00:09:37.596 --> 00:09:40.917
one hour a day to help free up my time.

00:09:40.917 --> 00:09:42.770
So you don't have to
jump to hiring somebody

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:46.169
for 50K starting salary full time.

00:09:46.169 --> 00:09:49.099
There are ways to get
volunteers, to get partners,

00:09:49.099 --> 00:09:52.210
to get people to help
you out, to get interns.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.463
You want to always be
keeping your ears open

00:09:54.463 --> 00:09:56.447
for potential talent,

00:09:56.447 --> 00:10:00.530
and start building your
team as soon as possible.

00:10:02.547 --> 00:10:04.580
And number seven is form
a great environment.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:07.446
I've talked about this a lot on my videos.

00:10:07.446 --> 00:10:09.662
It's probably going to
be a future book of mine

00:10:09.662 --> 00:10:11.290
at some point.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.505
Most people's environments just suck.

00:10:13.505 --> 00:10:15.306
Your environment keeps you where you are.

00:10:15.306 --> 00:10:17.322
We've talked about it how
many times in these videos.

00:10:17.322 --> 00:10:19.021
Have you changed your environment?

00:10:19.021 --> 00:10:20.588
Have you done it yet?

00:10:20.588 --> 00:10:21.993
Is it sinking in yet?

00:10:21.993 --> 00:10:25.218
What is on your wall at your
office where you are working?

00:10:25.218 --> 00:10:26.957
I don't care if it's in your basement.

00:10:26.957 --> 00:10:29.136
I don't care if it's at your mom's house.

00:10:29.136 --> 00:10:31.307
I don't care if you have an actual office.

00:10:31.307 --> 00:10:32.596
What is on the wall?

00:10:32.596 --> 00:10:35.526
Are you inspired going
there to work every day?

00:10:35.526 --> 00:10:37.336
What is you morning routine?

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:41.541
Do you do something every
day to get your mindset right

00:10:41.541 --> 00:10:44.086
to go out and believe in
that big thing you have?

00:10:44.086 --> 00:10:47.812
This video is about helping
you have a big impact.

00:10:47.812 --> 00:10:50.479
If you mind is not set properly,

00:10:51.349 --> 00:10:53.457
if you don't wake up every day thinking

00:10:53.457 --> 00:10:54.940
that you can have a big impact,

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.603
if you don't wake up every day motivated

00:10:56.603 --> 00:10:58.233
to want to go out and have a big impact,

00:10:58.233 --> 00:11:00.400
guess what's going to happen?

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:02.407
You're not going to have a big impact.

00:11:02.407 --> 00:11:05.180
'Cause that one afternoon
where you feel motivated

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:06.350
and encouraged, it's not enough.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.198
It's not sustainable.

00:11:08.198 --> 00:11:10.718
So think about the times when
you've been most motivated,

00:11:10.718 --> 00:11:13.282
most inspired, most dreaming big.

00:11:13.282 --> 00:11:14.518
What happened?

00:11:14.518 --> 00:11:15.510
Who were you talking to?

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:16.343
What were you consuming?

00:11:16.343 --> 00:11:17.176
What were you listening to?

00:11:17.176 --> 00:11:18.575
What were you watching?

00:11:18.575 --> 00:11:19.426
What was it?

00:11:19.426 --> 00:11:20.612
What happened in your life?

00:11:20.612 --> 00:11:23.811
And now inject that with
purpose every morning

00:11:23.811 --> 00:11:27.383
into your routine so
that you automatically

00:11:27.383 --> 00:11:30.716
every day wake up and you get motivation

00:11:31.946 --> 00:11:35.091
and you believe in that bigger
impact that you can have.

00:11:35.091 --> 00:11:36.588
It's so important guys,

00:11:36.588 --> 00:11:39.921
and I've talked about it
over and over and over again,

00:11:39.921 --> 00:11:42.122
and I don't see the action happen.

00:11:42.122 --> 00:11:44.410
And so I really want you to think about

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.732
what's on your walls,

00:11:45.732 --> 00:11:46.994
what your morning routine looks like,

00:11:46.994 --> 00:11:49.911
what your habits are and make some changes

00:11:49.911 --> 00:11:53.213
so that you can start
having the big impact

00:11:53.213 --> 00:11:56.182
that you can actually have.

00:11:56.182 --> 00:11:57.209
So that's what I got guys.

00:11:57.209 --> 00:12:00.070
Those are my seven ways that
you can have a big impact

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.044
as an entrepreneur.

00:12:01.044 --> 00:12:03.125
I'd love to know what did you think?

00:12:03.125 --> 00:12:04.481
What way was your favorite?

00:12:04.481 --> 00:12:06.333
What way did you agree with the most

00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:07.509
and resonated the most with?

00:12:07.509 --> 00:12:08.534
Did I miss something?

00:12:08.534 --> 00:12:09.564
Is there an eight, nine, ten

00:12:09.564 --> 00:12:11.535
that you guys want to add to the list?

00:12:11.535 --> 00:12:12.929
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:12.929 --> 00:12:14.896
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:14.896 --> 00:12:17.480
Finally I want to give a quick
shout out to Luca Avenali.

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.799
Luca, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:12:19.799 --> 00:12:20.882
Your One Word.

00:12:20.882 --> 00:12:23.013
It really really really means a lot to me.

00:12:23.013 --> 00:12:24.514
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:24.514 --> 00:12:25.701
I believe in you.

00:12:25.701 --> 00:12:27.698
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:27.698 --> 00:12:30.547
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:30.547 --> 00:12:32.964
Much love, I'll see you soon.

